There are a number of example R analyses at the distancesampling.org <http://distancesampling.org> website.  If you read through the example analysis of ducknests (http://distancesampling.org/R/vignettes/ducknests.html), that will get you started, although the ducknest data does not have clusters.  Also be advised that 5 transects is a small number to accurately estimate the variability in numbers of animals between transects; this is an important component in measuring the uncertainty in your abundance estimates.
