Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Olivier

As I understand the workings of ds(); if you specify an order for adjustment terms, there is no model selection performed; the model with specifically that series of adjustments is fitted.  By omitting the 'order' argument, ds() performs internal model selection working "bottom-up" beginning with no adjustment terms, increasing terms as necessary.  In normal use, the 'order' argument is seldom used.
ds(minke, key="hn", adjustment="cos", order=4)  results in

Adjustment term coefficient(s):
                estimate        se
cos, order 2  0.07515560 0.2124053
cos, order 3 -0.10036519 0.2182695
cos, order 4  0.05620197 0.1777044

By the way, I don't know how AIC made such a large change from your third to fourth fitted models.

