On 29/03/2017 10:25, Eric Rexstad wrote:
> Olivier
>
> As I understand the workings of ds(); if you specify an order for
> adjustment terms, there is no model selection performed; the model with
> specifically that series of adjustments is fitted.  By omitting the
> 'order' argument, ds() performs internal model selection working
> "bottom-up" beginning with no adjustment terms, increasing terms as
> necessary.  In normal use, the 'order' argument is seldom used.
>
